  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is heated with Conc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HI</mi></math> to give a hydroxy compound A which is further heated with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Zn</mi></math> dust to give compound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>. Identify <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0064_3b2fa3a92a66.png\" style=\"width: 376px; height: 80px;\" />​​​​​​​</p>"
