  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Alkyl aryl ethers are cleaved at the alkyl-oxygen bond due to the more stable aryl-oxygen bond. The reaction yields phenol and alkyl halide.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0064_c65119603063.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 113px;\" /></p><p>And then&nbsp;Phenol is converted to benzene on heating with zinc dust.<img src=\"assets\\st0064_9949bce6856b.png\" style=\"width: 538px; height: 80px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
